#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/saving_models.ipynb:540
msgid "Making edits to a serialised model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/saving_models.ipynb:542
msgid ""
"As mentioned at the begining of this notebook, only models which have "
"already been discretised can be serialised and readh back in. This means "
"that after serialisation, the model *cannot be edited*, as the non-"
"discretised elements of the model such as the original rhs are not saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/saving_models.ipynb:544
msgid ""
"If you are likely to want to save a model and then edit it in the future, "
"you may wish to use the ``Simulation.save()`` functionality to pickle your "
"simulation, as described in `tutorial 6 <https://github.com/pybamm-team/"
"PyBaMM/blob/main/docs/source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-6-"
"managing-simulation-outputs.ipynb>`__."
msgstr ""

